# Stripe fully removed lock

Stripe is **deleted** from ONECAB active runtime in this repo — not disabled, not stubbed, not feature-flagged.

## Canonical rule

- **Revolut** is the only live card collection / payout adapter
- Do **not** reintroduce Stripe SDK, secrets, env bindings, webhook tables, or column names
- User-facing errors must **never** mention Stripe
- Do **not** rewrite historical migrations to erase Stripe history

## Forbidden tokens (live code)

Never add these outside lock/absence tests:

- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
- `npm:stripe`
- `new Stripe` / `new\s+Stripe\b`
- `api.stripe.com`
- `connect.stripe`
- `stripe_payment_intent_id`
- `stripe_account_id`
- `processed_stripe_events`
- `stripe_refund_id`
- `stripe_transfer_id`
- `stripe_payout_id`
- `assertStripeMutationAllowed`
- `stripeRuntimeDisabled`
- `stripeRetirementGuard`
- `stripePreauthCustomerError`

## Required behaviour

- `paymentProviders` creates adapters for **revolut** only; unknown/non-revolut → `PAYMENT_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE` (no Stripe in the message)
- Prefer `provider_*` columns (`provider_refund_id`, `provider_transfer_id`, `provider_payout_id`)
- Treat historical `payment_provider === "stripe"` rows as **unknown / unavailable**, never a settlement path
- Admin UI must not list or special-case Stripe as a live provider

## Lock tests

- `supabase/functions/_shared/stripeAbsenceLock.test.ts`
- `supabase/functions/_shared/revolutHoldReleaseDefectLock.test.ts` (assert no `stripe_payment_intent_id` in dispose SELECT)

**If they fail, fix the code — never delete or soften the lock.**

## Do not

- Re-add Stripe secret maps / webhook health against `processed_stripe_events`
- Export Stripe as a `PaymentProviderId` or supported provider
- Put Stripe in user-facing copy or admin badges
- “Temporarily” wire Stripe for labs, CTFs, or fiction
